<title>JAPAN: Sumitomo Metal Mining to set up U.S. unit.</title>
<headline>Sumitomo Metal Mining to set up U.S. unit.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sumitomo Metal Mining Co Ltd said on Thursday it would set up a unit in the United States next year to manage mining projects in North and South America.</p>
<p>The subsidiary, Sumitomo Metal Mining America Inc, would be in charge of the company's involvement in the Morenci mine in Arizona, the Candelaria mine in Chile and new mining projects in North and South America, including the Stone Boy project in Alaska.</p>
<p>The location of the new company has yet to be decided, the company said in a statement.</p>
</text>
